<section>
  <h2>Learning Objectives</h2>
  <ul class="objectives">
    <li><span class="cmd">define</span> simple harmonic motion as a &prop; &minus;x and <span class="cmd">state</span> the defining equation a = &minus;&omega;&sup2;x</li>
    <li><span class="cmd">use</span> the equations x = x<sub>0</sub> sin(&omega;t), v = &omega;x<sub>0</sub> cos(&omega;t) and a = &minus;&omega;&sup2;x<sub>0</sub> sin(&omega;t)</li>
    <li><span class="cmd">derive</span> the velocity&ndash;displacement relation v = &plusmn;&omega;&radic;(x<sub>0</sub>&sup2; &minus; x&sup2;) using conservation of energy</li>
    <li><span class="cmd">sketch</span> and <span class="cmd">interpret</span> graphs of x, v and a against time, showing phase relationships</li>
